WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.516
The Patch Bay is the whole instrument as one hardware faceplate.

2
00:00:04.516 --> 00:00:05.947
Maximize it to see more.

3
00:00:06.403 --> 00:00:12.965
Along the top, the Sources bus offers signals: waveforms, audio, beats, MIDI, and more.

4
00:00:12.965 --> 00:00:17.641
Every parameter has an input jack, a knob, and an output jack.

5
00:00:18.093 --> 00:00:20.455
Cables run from an output to an input.

6
00:00:20.455 --> 00:00:26.549
Drag the triangle wave down onto Function Generator one, the same slot as in the Modulation panel.

7
00:00:26.549 --> 00:00:29.099
Near an edge, the board scrolls with you.

8
00:00:29.553 --> 00:00:30.459
Now its output.

9
00:00:30.459 --> 00:00:33.361
Grab the output jack, and carry it up to H Size.

10
00:00:33.812 --> 00:00:34.864
Restore the window.

11
00:00:34.864 --> 00:00:38.130
The raster now stretches in and out with the triangle wave.

12
00:00:38.728 --> 00:00:42.272
Back in the bay, grab a cable by its input end to move it.

13
00:00:42.272 --> 00:00:43.372
Drop it on V Size.

14
00:00:43.825 --> 00:00:46.286
Drop a cable in empty space to unplug it.

15
00:00:46.744 --> 00:00:51.181
Cables and the Modulation panel are two views of one patch.

16
00:00:51.181 --> 00:00:52.084
Next: nodes.
